{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["And the phrase לכל הבהמה also draws itself and another with it, for its sense is \"and to every bird of the sky,\" and likewise ויהי מתיו ממפר (Deuteronomy 33:6), and likewise ולא למדתי חכמה (Proverbs 30:3), and many like these." "And the sense of ולאדם לא מצא is ולנפשו לא מצא, for such is the usage of the blessed Name [Scripture], like וישלח ד' את ירבעל ואת בדן ואת יפתח ואת שמואל (1 Samuel 12:11). And it is far in my eyes that it [the matter] returns to the Name, and here it says that the bird was created from the earth, while above, from the waters, for from both it was created."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:18.679922531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}